# The security headers of the real screens on Cloudflare Pages (plan 5.9; platform facts 9.3).
# scripts/deploy/pages.sh writes dist/_headers from this file, with the hosts of one deployment, after the remote build.
# The prototype build never gets this file (scripts/check-bundles.ts). Lines that start with # stay out of dist/_headers.
#
# Placeholders (scripts/deploy/headers.ts):
#   {{SUPABASE}}      https://<ref>.supabase.co: Auth, Realtime, Storage uploads and the functions
#   {{SUPABASE_WSS}}  wss://<ref>.supabase.co: the Realtime socket
#   {{FILES}}         the host of the signed file links: the Supabase host while MADAR_FILE_STORE is supabase
#                     (proof Z0a, item 6), https://<account>.eu.r2.cloudflarestorage.com after the move to R2
# The fixed host https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org in connect-src is the place search of the pin picker (Task 12b, fbk_017).
# The fixed host https://tiles.openfreemap.org in connect-src is the street map: the tiles and the glyphs (owner, 2026-10-19). It is free,
# with no account and no key. The satellite tiles come from the own route /satellite (functions/satellite), so no Esri host is here.
# The fixed host https://eu.i.posthog.com in connect-src is PostHog Cloud EU (Frankfurt): usage data, errors and masked replays for the
# owner (insight design, 2026-10-25). The library loads no script from it, so script-src and worker-src need no change.
# The fixed host https://eu-assets.i.posthog.com in connect-src gives the settings of the project as JSON (/array/<token>/config): replays,
# clicks and the masking. Without it, PostHog keeps the replays and the click records off (test copy, 2026-10-25). No script comes from it.
# 'wasm-unsafe-eval' in script-src lets the Arabic text plugin of the map run its WebAssembly. It allows no eval().
# The map worker is the one exception (owner decision A, 2026-10-28, tsk_486). MapLibre loads the Arabic text plugin inside its worker: the
# worker fetches the plugin file as text and runs it with eval(), because the plugin is a classic script. The page policy blocks eval(),
# so the Arabic place names stayed unjoined. The rule of /assets/map-worker/* detaches the page policy ("! Name" removes a header that an
# earlier rule set: developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers, "Detach a header") and sets its own policy. That policy is the
# page policy plus 'unsafe-eval' in script-src, and nothing else. A dedicated worker takes its policy from the response of its own script
# file, so no page gets the looser policy. The rule must come after /* (the rules apply in file order) and the path must match the file
# that vite.config.ts writes (worker.rolldownOptions). scripts/deploy/headers.test.ts pins both policies and sends one policy to the file.
# style-src keeps 'unsafe-inline', because vaul adds a <style> element. img-src keeps blob: for the pictures of a new upload.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: {{FILES}}; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' {{SUPABASE}} {{SUPABASE_WSS}} {{FILES}} https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org https://tiles.openfreemap.org https://eu.i.posthog.com https://eu-assets.i.posthog.com; frame-src {{FILES}}; worker-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/map-worker/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' 'unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: {{FILES}}; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' {{SUPABASE}} {{SUPABASE_WSS}} {{FILES}} https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org https://tiles.openfreemap.org https://eu.i.posthog.com https://eu-assets.i.posthog.com; frame-src {{FILES}}; worker-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'

# The service worker of browser push (public/sw.js). The browser checks it for a new version on its own; no-cache makes it ask the
# server every time, so a fixed worker reaches the phones at once. The scope is the root, so the worker needs no extra header.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
